Source: pgextwlist
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-all (>= 217~)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/dimitri/pgextwlist

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-pgextwlist
Architecture: any
Depends: ${postgresql:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: PostgreSQL extension whitelisting
 pgextwlist allows administrators to control which extensions users may
 install and to run custom scripts around extension management commands.
 The module is enabled with local_preload_libraries or session_preload_libraries;
 it does not require CREATE EXTENSION.
